/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees\/treap"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The random priorities make the shape that of a random binary search tree, whatever order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements arrive in, so lookup, insertion and removal take O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected time. A treap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also splits at an element into the elements below it and the rest, and joins two treaps whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements don’t interleave. The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed by rank like an array: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"treap[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The priorities come from a random number generator given at creation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The treap draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"priorities as its original."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the treap holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}]}]}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Treap.swift","